    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of braces instead of parentheses in Scala for comprehensions to avoid the need for semicolons at the end of lines.",
    "explanation" : "# For Brace\n\nUsage of braces (rather than parentheses) within a `for` comprehension mean that you don't have to specify a semi-colon at the end of every line:\n\n```scala\nfor { // braces\n  t <- List(1,2,3)\n  if (t % 2 == 0)\n} yield t\n```\n\nis preferred to\n\n```scala\nfor ( // parentheses\n  t <- List(1,2,3);\n  if (t % 2 == 0)\n) yield t\n```\n\nTo fix it, replace the `()` with `{}`. And then remove the `;` at the end of the lines.",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
